  "method": "Retail instruction bytes for the selected function were executed under unicorn 2.1.4 (x86-32) with the true PE image mapped at 0x00400000 and a synthetic cdecl stack; the candidate C++ implementation was compiled and executed natively with the same synthetic state; return values, context fields, and copied bytes were compared. Unicorn is used for isolated retail-byte execution, rather than a live Windows game process, and because x87 (fptan/fld/fmul/fdiv/fstp) is not implemented by Radare2 ESIL or angr VEX.",
